{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1323873-supernatural-hauntings-and-ghost-curses-not-represented-by-wraith","id":1323873,"title":"Supernatural Hauntings and Ghost Curses not represented by Wraith","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-11T23:35:22-07:00","id":1323873,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Supernatural Hauntings and Ghost Curses not represented by Wraith","content":"So one of the problems, minor problem, I have is we need more examples or methods of odd hauntings and what not you can't replicate easily with the Wraith rules. Things like say modern horror like Samara from the Ring, a lot of it could be represented with Pandemonium and what not but creating those scary videos, dwelling in a Pocket Dimension of the Well and Physically turning the Television into a portal.<br /> <br /> And weird elemental curses like those who died in a fire controlling flame or having Demonic minions made of flame. Weird Immortal Dead/Revenant myths like when Odin cursed an Army to return from death over and over. Just weird odd ghost story stuff.<br /> <br /> You can handle it with handwaving by saying Plasmics could exist that could do it, and that could be interesting and would be nice to have more examples of mysterious Plasmics that dwell in the Shadowland rather then the Tempest, Tindel Hounds are great after all.<br /> <br /> Oddly I find Changeling and Mage better at representing certain Hauntings and ghost stories. One of the strengths I found with Geist was they were pretty good at the weird ghost powers allowing you to Freddy Krueger people (Sandman can do this) and replicate Tales from the Crypt style Twists.<br /> <br /> How do others handle certain ghost stories and curses not easily represented by Wraith?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T02:29:36-07:00","id":1323893,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I tend to had wave a lot of it if not involved in a fight with the PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T04:48:03-07:00","id":1323914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1323873-supernatural-hauntings-and-ghost-curses-not-represented-by-wraith?p=1323893#post1323893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I tend to had wave a lot of it if not involved in a fight with the PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's the current method for weirdness, either handwave (like they do with Ancient Ghost's systemless might) or do a crossover.<br /> <br /> But with that in mind for Crossovers I've made a Selkie Queen whose whooed mortals and unleashed magic upon a the ghost of a dead lover to cast him and his sword forever in Faery Fire. And enchanting ghostly goods for her mortal souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T18:51:20-07:00","id":1324101,"title":"","content":"Samara?<br /> <br /> Inhabit to possess and control tv\u2019s, videos etc. And to ride the electric Highway to the television in question if need be.<br /> <br /> Embody, or with Wr20 Pandemonium, to manifest from the TV and attack the victim. Also Embody in Wr20 could help one pull the victim to your well, that is into Shadowlands.<br /> <br /> Pandemonium for the flies, water and other manifestations and odd phenomenon happening, like in Rings the rain falling upwards.<br /> <br /> Lifeweb to splice strand into the tape for easier following and acting around it.<br /> <br /> Possibly Usury to drain the life of a victim and this explaining why they appear as they do.<br /> <br /> That should cover most of the things Samara does in Ring movies.<br /> <br /> There are some differences between that and what Sadako does in the original Ringu movies but those Arcanoi could help with them as well.<br /> <br /> Remember though that Samara/Sadako is quite clearly a Spectre and thus has access to Dark Arcanoi as well for added effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T20:58:46-07:00","id":1324131,"title":"","content":"Those are good points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T02:20:34-07:00","id":1324170,"title":"","content":"As for elemental ghosts who died by fire, for example, it\u2019s mostly through Outrage/Pandemonium. Outrage is able to cause fires though control is beyond it, but creative uses of Pandemonium may help in controlling it, make flammables less so as they are soaked in foul liquids Etc.<br /> <br /> Controlled fires and even demonic fire beings can be conjured through a combination of Embody/Phantasm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T21:50:05-07:00","id":1383089,"title":"","content":"Regarding The Ring, the American version implies that she may have been not entirely human, and IIRC, the original Japanese novel is almost explicit that she is not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T14:04:36-07:00","id":1383212,"title":"","content":"Yeah, wasn't Sadako's father more or less stated to be some kind of sea demon in the original film?<br /> <br /> I could also see an argument that the whole &quot;Hell is real&quot; aspect implies infernal powers at work rather than ghostly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T14:17:29-07:00","id":1383217,"title":"","content":"Wasn't she hermaphroditic in the original literature, and something something Universal Metavirus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T18:49:19-07:00","id":1383266,"title":"","content":"It's been a few years since I've read the novel, but I believe the answer is yes to both. (It gave some specific term for her condition, but I forget what it was, or even if it was a real thing.)<br /> I need to read the rest of the trilogy at some point.<br /> <br /> As for odd haunting effects, I'm still trying to figure out how you'd do the end of Poltergiest in Wraith other than ST fiat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T00:09:50-07:00","id":1383523,"title":"","content":"There's certainly a lot <span style=\"font-family:arial\">of classical hauntings that aren't addressed </span>by Wraith. It was something I gave a lot of though too once. I'll share some of them here if people are interested. Just comment and discuss, and I'll share more.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Automatic Writing</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Phenomenon: The living enter a trance where they unconsciously write messages from those beyond the Shroud. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">WoD Explanation: Many cases are due to the use of the Puppetry Arcanoi. However, in some cases the Shadow of the living has accessed the Hive Mind. Some individuals have an instinctive Merit to access this, while others only develop it due to continued attunement by Puppeteers until it occurs instinctively. What messages are delivered by Automatic Writing is determined by both the living\u2019s subconscious or conscious desires and whatever inscrutable warnings the Hive Mind wishes to deliver. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T01:34:54-07:00","id":1383532,"title":"","content":"By all means share. One thing I think that could be useful is a power to have semiautonomous like plasmic entities. Like a Pandemonium/Phantasm or Embody Alloyed Arcanos that makes things that creep around the shadows of mortal perceptions, or sentient willowisps or man faced rats like Dreams in a Witches house.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T19:03:53-07:00","id":1383705,"title":"","content":"I've never gone down the path of having any power to create a semi-autonomous plasmic entity. I'd just use some weird moliated mind blown Spectre, or use some kind of actual plasmic entity that somehow crossed over. It's just the matter of determining the gimmick that allows that temporary kind of Shroud crossing. Perhaps a curse artifact, or a special plot device for a certain Nephwrack cult.<br /> <br /> Here's the next one.<br /> <br /> B<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>lack Dogs</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Phenomenon: Many cultures throughout the ages have ongoing myths detail about spectral black dogs associated with death. They have various names in different times and cultures such as barghests, shucks, spectral hounds, or black dogs. They usually appear in lonely country lanes or cemeteries. Their appearance in the Skinlands are taken as omens of death. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">WoD Explanation: Many of these dogs are in fact barghests: moliated Wraiths, given the appearance of dogs, that serve the Hierarchy. However, some are actually plasmic creatures called Deliriums and Phantasies. (Some of these, like the fabled pale horses of the Equitae, are in the service of highly-placed Hierarchs.) Black dog appearances may have mundane causes (Hierarchy hunting parties cross the Shroud at the right time and place to hunt criminals, or p</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">erhaps the Legion of Faith has special plasmic creatures in their service that &quot;track&quot; humans fated to die and lead the Legion's reapers to them</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">) or weirder ones (the wishes of Fate or Oblivion causes Phantasies to cross over as omens of the ST's plot involving death in the Skinlands, or activites of Spectres).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Skinland areas of repeated reports of black dogs may indicate the presence of frequent Legion patrols, or Nihils that attract plasmic creatures from the Tempest, combined with a special reason why they manifest in the Skinlands. Perhaps the Shroud is particularly weak or non-existent there at certain times, or the Skinlands area is known as a place where the Dictum Mortem is routinely violated and special legionary patrols are allowed to break the Shround in order to appehend the criminals.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 04-25-2020, 03:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T00:06:17-07:00","id":1383728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1323873-supernatural-hauntings-and-ghost-curses-not-represented-by-wraith?p=1383705#post1383705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never gone down the path of having any power to create a semi-autonomous plasmic entity. I'd just use some weird moliated mind blown Spectre, or use some kind of actual plasmic entity that somehow crossed over. It's just the matter of determining the gimmick that allows that temporary kind of Shroud crossing. Perhaps a curse artifact, or a special plot device for a certain Nephwrack cult.<br /> <br /> Here's the next one.<br /> <br /> B<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>lack Dogs</b></span></span></span> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Phenomenon: Many cultures throughout the ages have ongoing myths detail about spectral black dogs associated with death. They have various names in different times and cultures such as barghests, shucks, spectral hounds, or black dogs. They usually appear in lonely country lanes or cemeteries. Their appearance in the Skinlands are taken as omens of death. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">WoD Explanation: Many of these dogs are in fact barghests: moliated Wraiths, given the appearance of dogs, that serve the Hierarchy. However, some are actually plasmic creatures called Deliriums and Phantasies. (Some of these, like the fabled pale horses of the Equitae, are in the service of highly-placed Hierarchs.) Black dog appearances may have mundane causes (Hierarchy hunting parties cross the Shroud at the right time and place to hunt criminals, or p</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">erhaps the Legion of Faith has special plasmic creatures in their service that &quot;track&quot; humans fated to die and lead the Legion's reapers to them</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">) or weirder ones (the wishes of Fate or Oblivion causes Phantasies to cross over as omens of the ST's plot involving death in the Skinlands, or activites of Spectres).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Skinland areas of repeated reports of black dogs may indicate the presence of frequent Legion patrols, or Nihils that attract plasmic creatures from the Tempest, combined with a special reason why they manifest in the Skinlands. Perhaps the Shroud is particularly weak or non-existent there at certain times, or the Skinlands area is known as a place where the Dictum Mortem is routinely violated and special legionary patrols are allowed to break the Shround in order to appehend the criminals.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>...and sometimes they're Silent Strider Ahroun sample characters from a tribebook!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T02:15:37-07:00","id":1383738,"title":"","content":"Not all the things have to be wraith related either. It could be Umbral spirit related. Most humans would say that they were haunted though as they are not cosmologists and most people are also not animistic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T11:10:56-07:00","id":1383802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1323873-supernatural-hauntings-and-ghost-curses-not-represented-by-wraith?p=1383738#post1383738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all the things have to be wraith related either. It could be Umbral spirit related. Most humans would say that they were haunted though as they are not cosmologists and most people are also not animistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yes but I mean if I wanted to tell it in a wraith game. Though in my opinion I would have more umbral bleed over in wraith. Like with the Yin Yang and Yomi mirrorlands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T19:32:44-07:00","id":1383894,"title":"","content":"I think in a Wraith game that things should be Wraith centric, just like anytime you run a game in any system it should be centered on that. At the very least, in-character things should be explainable in terms of how those characters understand things in their milieu.<br /> <br /> At one point in time, I was very exclusive in how each layer of the Umbra was divided, but now I am much more open to figuring out ways how creatures and people can voyage throughout the spirit worlds. So some amount of inter-umbral travel is appropriate in my view.<br /> <br /> Here's the next.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Electronic Voice Phenomenon (EVP)</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Phenomenon: Sound recording equipment left alone in haunted places record bizarre, strange noises when there should be no sound recorded at all given the time and location. After being manipulated, these recordings sometimes reveal actual words, or at least sounds that exhibit speech patterns, or other signs of intelligence. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">WoD Explanation: Much EVP phenomenon is either false or faked, but sometimes it is real. EVP picks up the background noise of the Tempest or local Shadowlands, a random phenomenon that happens after a significant time has passed at the last presence of human life. All cases require a low Shroud rating. In the case of noise from the Tempest, the ST may determine a temporary Nihil has formed in order to allow any noise to pass through. ST may decide to allow something of importance (like a spectral plot through the Hive Mind, or an overheard conversation of Renegades temporarily staying over at the Haunt) to reach the Skinlands for plot purposes.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T19:58:19-07:00","id":1383899,"title":"","content":"I remember the early introductory stuff for Atlanta including something about a relic radio station that may have sometimes bled over into living broadcasts, I think. I always wish there'd been more follow up on technology and science in the underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T03:42:38-07:00","id":1383932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1323873-supernatural-hauntings-and-ghost-curses-not-represented-by-wraith?p=1383899#post1383899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember the early introductory stuff for Atlanta including something about a relic radio station that may have sometimes bled over into living broadcasts, I think. I always wish there'd been more follow up on technology and science in the underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah I wish there were more just bizarre ghost phenomena. Probably why I love haunters.<br /> <br /> <br /> I wonder how to represent things like horror movie spectors like Freddy Krueger wanting to eat souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T09:58:19-07:00","id":1383971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1323873-supernatural-hauntings-and-ghost-curses-not-represented-by-wraith?p=1383932#post1383932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how to represent things like horror movie spectors like Freddy Krueger wanting to eat souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Phantasm arcanos, augmented with Outrage, does most of the Nightmare on Elm Street stuff. Phantasm 5: Agon allows one to rip a soul from its body, while Usury allows one to steal Pathos and Corpus from souls. Also the Dark Arcanos called Larceny (or Leechcraft in Wraith: The Great War), which allows one to both steal Corpus and gain Angst from inflicting aggravated damage to others. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T12:20:00-07:00","id":1383993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1323873-supernatural-hauntings-and-ghost-curses-not-represented-by-wraith?p=1383971#post1383971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Phantasm arcanos, augmented with Outrage, does most of the Nightmare on Elm Street stuff. Phantasm 5: Agon allows one to rip a soul from its body, while Usury allows one to steal Pathos and Corpus from souls. Also the Dark Arcanos called Larceny (or Leechcraft in Wraith: The Great War), which allows one to both steal Corpus and gain Angst from inflicting aggravated damage to others. </div> </div> </div> </div>There we go I knew they had this one. Just thinking of nightmare on elm street I think five when Freddy turned souls into meatballs on a pizza and ate them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T13:08:44-07:00","id":1384250,"title":"","content":"This is something that doesn't get much observation now, but it is a very old type of haunting. I use its German name here, but other cultures have their own terms. In Ireland, it is called a fetch.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Dopplegangers (bilocation)</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Phenomenon: While White Wolf has used the term Doppleganger to refer to a wraith permanently consumed by their Shadow, it also has an older meaning - the \u201cdouble walker.\u201d A doppelganger is a shadow-self of a human, a phantasm of the living. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Typically it only appears before the owner of a doppelganger, but there are exceptions. It sometimes manifests in a mirror or other reflective surface, although it casts no reflection on its own. Dogs and cats have been known to sense doppelgangers. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">These types of apparition are often mistaken for the ghost of a dead person. Some think that the doppelganger is an etheric counterpart of the physical body that is reserved for the purpose of carrying the soul after death. Occasionally, in times of illness or great distress, it would seem that this ethereal replica is somehow projected or detached from its physical counterpart through some mysterious process. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Many famous people have reported this baffling phenomenon - Queen Elizabeth and Johann Wolfgang Goethe are two examples. The doppelganger has even been projected over considerable distances to materialize in full view of witnesses. It is said to be bad luck if it is seen, and rarely a doppelganger becomes visible to friends or family, often causing great confusion. It is often an omen of impending death.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The fear of the double is observed, if unknowingly, in the custom of covering all the mirrors in a house where a death has just occurred. The double of anyone passing the glass, it was once thought, could be projected into the mirror, and carried off by the deceased to the afterworld. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">WoD Explanation: Dopplegangers are the awakened Shadow in possession of the soul\u2019s plasmic body manifested or embodied in the Skinlands while the person is still alive. The Shadow is not typically \u201cawake\u201d until the passage of death activates it by the closer proximity to Oblivion. However, there may be times when still alive that one\u2019s Shadow, the unconscious, reaches out. The Doppleganger sometime materializes only to its owner, and might not be seen by anyone else. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Shadow projects usually for two reasons. One is that it senses the approach of Oblivion because the person will soon die, and its projection is a premonition of doom. The second is truly rare, occurring only when the subject has intense emotion, desire, or passion when thinking about another person or place. The living person fuels the Shadow with such Pathos/Angst that it is able to project in the location of the place or person. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Because of the non-euclidean geometry of the Tempest, this projection could conceivably be anywhere. The double instinctively attempts to connect with the source of such Passion. However, the amount of Pathos/Angst needed to fuel this is so high that the double is not maintained for long. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Some practitioners of black magic are able to consciously project their double. After falling asleep or entering a trance, the double goes forth to wreak havoc in the world of the living. This could be mirrored by a Merit, a Demonic Investment, or perhaps a rite with one of the Paths of Sorcery like Ephemera.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T16:19:22-07:00","id":1384734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for odd haunting effects, I'm still trying to figure out how you'd do the end of Poltergiest in Wraith other than ST fiat. </div> </div> </div>Would it be possible for a single powerful wraith to use either Tesseract Bomb or Obliviate in combination with/sequentially with Harrow the Mortal Flesh to tear a house apart/fold it in on itself and pull it across the shroud?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T17:39:28-07:00","id":1384743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1323873-supernatural-hauntings-and-ghost-curses-not-represented-by-wraith?p=1384734#post1384734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would it be possible for a single powerful wraith to use either Tesseract Bomb or Obliviate in combination with/sequentially with Harrow the Mortal Flesh to tear a house apart/fold it in on itself and pull it across the shroud?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like something a Malfean could maybe do but Wraith powers don\u2019t go up to 11.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T23:47:03-07:00","id":1384789,"title":"","content":"Poltergeist is really over the top in terms of ghost stories. Real world ghost stories (actual ghostly encounters people have reported) don't have anything like that. Even legends and fictional ghost stories are typically more down to earth - not leaving much evidence that it happened. So it needs some sort of plot device that explains how a house could have blown up.<br /> <br /> If I had to actually narrate the first movie in Wraith terms, I'd likely have the Beast be some kind of Nephwrack or other horror, and that it was an intervention by one of the Legions off camera that destroyed it, and they used some kind of special device to shock the Shroud back into existence which is the implosion the family saw - the house was so Oblivion tainted at that point that it belonged &quot;more&quot; into the Shadowlands than the Skinlands. Likely, I'd have Wraith PCs be skinriding the family during the movie in order to learn what is happening in the Skinlands so they can report back to the local Necropolis what is happening and the level of the threat so that the Legion can adequately prepare to fight the Beast. <br /> <br /> I'd introduce the PCs by having them keep tabs on parapsychologists and mediums as part of the Legions recon on possible violations of the Dictum Mortem. So when they go to investigate the house, that's when the scenario begins for the PCs who then begin to learn about the nature of the activity.<br /> <br /> Here's another version of hauntings that Wraith does not properly address.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">H<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>auntings, residual</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Phenomenon: In a residual or non-intelligent haunting, a scene is played out like a tape recorder. It repeats itself again and again whenever &quot;played back&quot;. It is theorized that the phenomenon is from a \u201cpsychic impression\u201d because very strong emotions can theoretically leave an imprint in time. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">For example a house may have had a man fall down the stairs. Sounds of somebody falling down the stairs are now heard often in the house. This is most likely a residual haunting. Residual hauntings are distinct from &quot;intelligent hauntings&quot; which indicate some amount of free-will of the ghost, or interaction between the ghost and the living. While intelligent hauntings may have common themes, they do not have the repetition of residual hauntings.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">WoD Explantion: Many residual hauntings are drones: mindless wraiths without enough willpower for conscious action. However, some residual hauntings have other causes. Since many drones are reaped and sent to the soul forges, such residual hauntings would cease if this was the sole explanation. While not all drones are found and reaped, any activity prolonged enough to attract attention of ghost hunters would certainly be noticed by Reapers as well. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">In such cases, one solution is that the physical location itself is fueled with Pathos caused by the Passions of the living about a specific incident or set of events. Manifestations occur by spontaneous Wylding as if through the Pandemonium Arcanos. Such \u201chaunted locations\u201d might even bedevil wraiths and be beyond their power to control. Such places might be actively policed by the Hierarchy. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Another solution is that such Haunting occur when a place serves both as a Haunt and Fetter for wraiths. The combination spontaneously provides such effects.<br /> <br /> Another explanation is that intelligent wraiths relive the acts that fuel their Passions. Maybe their Passions are very specific, or such acts are crucial to maintain one\u2019s Memoriam or Legacy.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 04-30-2020, 02:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T16:51:39-07:00","id":1384957,"title":"","content":"Great haunting ideas, Black Fox! Thanks for them, and if you have more, please do share!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T18:18:22-07:00","id":1385161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1323873-supernatural-hauntings-and-ghost-curses-not-represented-by-wraith?p=1384743#post1384743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like something a Malfean could maybe do but Wraith powers don\u2019t go up to 11.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, Reverend Kane had a whole cult of followers and in the second movie his appearance as &quot;the Beast&quot; looked like he'd consumed them and made them part of himself. That fits the bill of a Onceborn Malfean pretty well, though he'd have to be a very recent one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T23:02:44-07:00","id":1385197,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\">This is a phenomenon that some games already have explanations for. So this is already easily simulated, but this is putting it in perspective of use within a Wraith game.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Old Hag</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Phenomenon: Psychologists have recognized 'Old Hag Syndrome', or sleep paralysis, for many years. Scientists believe it is simply the product of a half-awake mind, but there are those who believe the cause is supernatural. Victims wake up in bed to find that they cannot move, even though they can see, hear, feel and smell. They often experience the feeling of a great weight on their chest and sense that there is a sinister or evil presence in the room. This presence sometimes manifests itself as an old hag with evil-looking eyes, hence the name of this syndrome. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">WoD Explanation: No doubt some occurrences have mundane causes, but this does not make for exciting roleplay. In fact, Hags do exist and prey on humanity while it sleeps. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Hags are a type of Tempest creature like Legendaries. The Malfean Lachesis also has Oblivion-ravaged spectres called Hags. Both collect souls, and sometimes attempt to claim those of the living. They attack through use of the Arcanoi Phantasm and Usury. Either or both could be responsible for the phenomenon.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Hags desire the vitality of young adults, but rarely have the power. Instead, they prey most effectively against the elderly and children, especially newborn babies. The Hierarchy knows of such creatures and views them as servants of Oblivion.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 05-02-2020, 03:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T23:58:42-07:00","id":1385205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1323873-supernatural-hauntings-and-ghost-curses-not-represented-by-wraith?p=1385197#post1385197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">This is a phenomenon that some games already have explanations for. So this is already easily simulated, but this is putting it in perspective of use within a Wraith game.</span> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Old Hag</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Phenomenon: Psychologists have recognized 'Old Hag Syndrome', or sleep paralysis, for many years. Scientists believe it is simply the product of a half-awake mind, but there are those who believe the cause is supernatural. Victims wake up in bed to find that they cannot move, even though they can see, hear, feel and smell. They often experience the feeling of a great weight on their chest and sense that there is a sinister or evil presence in the room. This presence sometimes manifests itself as an old hag with evil-looking eyes, hence the name of this syndrome. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">WoD Explanation: No doubt some occurrences have mundane causes, but this does not make for exciting roleplay. In fact, Hags do exist and prey on humanity while it sleeps. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Hags are a type of Tempest creature like Legendaries. The Malfean Lachesis also has Oblivion-ravaged spectres called Hags. Both collect souls, and sometimes attempt to claim those of the living. They attack through use of the Arcanoi Phantasm and Usury. Either or both could be responsible for the phenomenon.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Hags desire the vitality of young adults, but rarely have the power. Instead, they prey most effectively against the elderly and children, especially newborn babies. The Hierarchy knows of such creatures and views them as servants of Oblivion.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>See this is why I want the setting to have more Plasmics. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T00:12:56-07:00","id":1385208,"title":"","content":"I agree that Plasmics are a great resource for any Wraith ST. Sea of Shadows does a great job conceptualizing them and organizing them into categories, but really needed to provide more specific creatures that fit the setting. Perhaps once I exhaust my list of normal hauntings, I'll post types of Plasmics I think should be in the game. It's not really a &quot;Haunting&quot;, but many are based in lore or fiction about the afterlife or the world beyond.<br /> <br /> Another thing I think travel in the Tempest requires is that most hoary of old school RPG concepts - the wandering monster/encounter table that includes different wraiths, plasmics, and zones. It wouldn't be used in typical D&amp;D fashion in terms of X minutes go by, roll on the table. But to help organize different areas of the Tempest thematically so we know what kinds of encounters predominate in those areas, and it would help differentiate them. Such a table would actually be a very efficient way to distinguish between different Tempest areas. And for an ST running an extended Tempest voyage, it would help him determine what kind of events happen along the way regardless if he rolls randomly or picks his own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T21:16:30-07:00","id":1385732,"title":"","content":"Sorcerer Revised for Mage (although I do not understand why the Revised edition for Sorcerer was for the Mage line while the original was a generic World of Darkness. The book is needed much more for the other game lines.) has Ectoplasmic Generation as a Psychic ability, but that may not be sufficient for certain occurrences an ST would want in a Wraith game.<br /> <br /> For actual mechanics you may want to use that or handwave things as being a Merit if you just want to explain an NPC with the abilities. While the phenomenon is associated with Victorian era with scam artists (I think I read that the ectoplasmic entities were made from cheese cloth), I always remember its used in the Hellboy story <a href=\"https://hellboy.fandom.com/wiki/Goodbye_Mister_Tod\" target=\"_blank\">Goodbye, Mr Tod</a>.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Mediums, Physical</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Phenomenon: In the early days of the spiritual movement, some mediums claimed to be able to physically manifest the spirits in a weird semi-corporeal substance called ectoplasm. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">WoD Explanation: Most ectoplasmic phenomena is faked, but a very rare few individuals are capable of it. Much like Benandanti born with intact cauls, physical mediums have within them a formed plasmic corpus. These mediums can instinctively choose to become a consort of contacted spirits who can embody in the Skinlands by instinctive moliation of the plasmic corpus across the Shroud. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">This is extraordinarily dangerous for the medium. Certain hostile entities - whether spectres or plasmic Wyrds - may try to fully materialize with their full powers. While in such a state, these creatures cannot only use their own powers, but can also drain the necessary Pathos from the physical medium as well. In addition, the amount of plasm contained in the physical medium may be insufficient for certain sizes of materialization. If the entire amount of plasm is used, the physical medium dies. The ectoplasm is highly sensitive, and if touched or exposed to light, the ectoplasm may inflict Health Levels of damage on the medium as it turns to dust.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T21:21:41-07:00","id":1385734,"title":"","content":"See this is why I really wish we had Sorcerer Revised as a resource for all the gamelines, but they push it into the background. If I was going to do a Classic World of Darkness Core I would put pretty Much Sorcerer Revised rules in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T16:12:57-07:00","id":1385961,"title":"","content":"One thing I should mention at this point is that one concept I use for some of these hauntings concerns the Shadow of the living. I've mentioned it in previous posts. It's mentioned again in this one, and will be used again in the future. So what do I mean by it?<br /> <br /> The living possesses Shadows, just as wraiths do. The difference is that the Shadow is usually not active. The conscious mind is not able to deal with all of the options and information available to it. Consciousness struggles to narrow and focus its energy to avoid drowning in endless possibility. So, consciousness selects certain stimuli, options, or patterns, and shuts out the rest for its own good. Everything else still remains within the unconscious mind, the province of the Shadow. <br /> <br /> The Shadow is the faculty in the unconscious mind that understands and adduces further information from these patterns on many higher levels. The unconscious mind, with its superior grasp of the causal world, and the tremendous sway it has over whim and attention span, could bring highly unusual experiences to the conscious mind under these circumstances. In a real sense, the Shadow is better informed than the Psyche, which has the tendency to forget or ignore information and memories that are unwanted. <br /> <br /> People do things all the time for which they have no rational explanation. People engage in all sorts of self-destructive acts despite the warnings and pleas from loved ones. The death urge is strong. Existence is a constant struggle, and the lure of Oblivion is that it promises final peace. <br /> <br /> Only in death, once the Psyche crosses the Shroud, does the Shadow rise to the surface to argue with the Psyche actively. This activation is caused by the Wraith\u2019s closer proximity to Oblivion. Where once before the Shadow could only act unconsciously, it can now take a more active role in asserting itself against the Psyche. <br /> <br /> The Shadows of those in the Skinlands will rarely come into play. Without a closer proximity to Oblivion caused by death and appearance in the Underworld, the Shadow does not have enough power to become an active force. However, while the struggle against Oblivion\u2019s siren call assumes epic proportions in the Underworld, that call sometimes also crosses the Shroud to reach the living. <br /> <br /> However, the Shadow also serves as a conduit to other supernatural agencies. It has a connection to the Tempest, which is a depository of the collective unconscious; It is said that anything lost in the Skinlands finds itself as part of the Tempest, including memories, knowledge, and hopes. It is also linked to the Hive Mind of the Shadow-eaten. It is not true that only the Dead struggle with their Shadow. The conflict is merely brought out into the open in the Shadowlands. It is the key that allows Oblivion to enter the Skinlands through dreams or paranormal phenomenon in the waking world.<br /> <br /> So with that said, I now present the Ouija Board. How does it actually work?<br /> <br /> <b>Ouija Boards </b><br /> <br /> Phenomenon: This parlor game allows communication with unseen spirits by normal, untrained people. A marker - called a planchette -moves without conscious action by the ones touching it. The board itself typically lists each letter of the alphabet, the numerals 0-9, the words \u201cYes\u201d and \u201cNo\u201d, and the phrase \u201cGood Bye.\u201d Many commercially made boards are available, but home made ones work equally as well sometimes with more symbols or words. Ouija Boards have existed in various forms since Antiquity.<br /> <br /> WoD Explanation: Sometimes wraiths are drawn to the Ouija Board and act with their Arcanoi. The commitment by the mortal users in the Skinlands temporarily lowers the Shroud around them. <br /> <br /> This is not the sole explanation though. We cannot assume that every time someone uses a Ouija Board that there is always a wraith who freely chooses to attend. We need an explanation can always account for Ouija activity. <br /> <br /> The Ouija Board is a mystical tool: crude but effective. It actually serves as a way to activate the unconscious mind of its participants. This is called the Shadow, which is dormant among the living. The Shadow cannot truly act, but it can serve as a conduit for the collective unconscious found in the Tempest, and specifically can contact the Hive Mind of spectres. These spectres can manipulate such unconscious movements of the planchette by communication with the person\u2019s Shadow, or in very dangerous cases consciously direct the movements themselves via their Arcanoi, just like wraiths. <br /> <br /> If the living call a specific wraith, that wraith\u2019s Shadow is likewise contacted and nudges the Psyche to arrive at the location or seeks Catharsis in order to respond. Sometimes no wraiths or spectres are contacted at all. It is simply the Shadow of the living, having been empowered, that causes the body to unconsciously move the planchette to reveal the answers discovered through the Hive Mind.<br /> <br /> The Ouija Board can become dangerous for its users. Not only does it lower the Shroud, but it acts as attunement for the spirits it contacts. Thus its users can become Consorts. Since the Ouija Board more often contacts the Hive Mind of Spectres than wraiths, prolonged use increases the danger to its participants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T22:04:00-07:00","id":1386254,"title":"","content":"Alrighty so I'll first freely admit that of the core five gamelines Wraith is probably the one I have the least concrete grasp on and it's probably just ahead of Reckoning and Mummy in general.<br /> <br /> Yet as I was reading over this thread, one that I enjoy a lot, an idea came to me from the style of Black Fox's posts and I figured I'd add on.<br /> <br /> So without further ado...<br /> <br /> THE VANISHING HITCHHIKER<br /> <br /> \u2022Phenomena: Traveler's have reported meeting strange and mysterious wanderers for millennia. Shadows haunting roadways, specters asking for drives to places that no longer exist, invisible hands wrestling for steering wheels.<br /> <br /> \u2022WoD Explanation: Occasionally these hauntings are exactly what you would expect. Stretches of road where the veil is thin and allows wraiths to cross over, most often drones lurking along the same pathways.<br /> <br /> Sometimes however these are more then simple wraiths fettered by a desire to reach someplace they can never truly go. Some are professional traveler's who carry messages or reach out to lost fetters, tying themselves to traveler's to do so. Such professionals are rare though.<br /> <br /> Aside from recurring ghosts (such as the figure or figures known as 'Resurrection Mary' in Chicago) or one-time manifestations of travelers, there are also more chilling stories. Fighting for steering wheels with phantom hands or specters being struck down by cars and then vanishing. Haunting traveler's like blood on a fender.<br /> <br /> These are sometimes genuine Specters. Those who have managed to cross the veil and try to drag more souls into Oblivion by delivering death and destruction. Others reach out to the Subliminal Shadow and cause it to nudge the wheel. Others even try to create collisions along certain stretches of road to 'curse' them and then the veil enough for anyone to cross over to the Skinlands.<br /> <br /> The nature and circumstances may change but phantoms of all sorts haunt roads. Many seeking a destination they can't ever bare to see...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T22:44:20-07:00","id":1386617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1323873-supernatural-hauntings-and-ghost-curses-not-represented-by-wraith?p=1386254#post1386254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alrighty so I'll first freely admit that of the core five gamelines Wraith is probably the one I have the least concrete grasp on and it's probably just ahead of Reckoning and Mummy in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>I originally had a hard time getting into Wraith because I couldn't imagine what you'd actually do in a chronicle. For a long time I simply called the Wraith corebook &quot;the Big Book of NPCs&quot; because I couldn't imagine anything other than to use it to spice up one of the other game lines briefly. Then I had a friend who explained it to me very well, and I became intrigued and read the corebook in depth for the very first time and I got it. It's an extremely well conceived setting, and I think its first edition corebook is far the best of any of first edition corebooks.<br /> <br /> Yet I've never run a chronicle because nobody I know is interested in playing in it at all, not even for a short term chronicle. So it's really still just the Big Book of NPCs to me.<br /> <br /> But as good as it is, that doesn't mean they couldn't have done some things better in terms of real hauntings.<br /> <br /> <b>Poltergeists </b><br /> <br /> Phenomenon: Poltergeists are commonly blamed for any violent or destructive activity in a haunting. In the past, researchers believed that all such activity at a haunted location was the work of spirits or another outside force, but today many investigators don\u2019t. The current theory behind Poltergeist phenomena is that the activity is caused by a person in the household, known as the \u201chuman agent\u201d. The agent is usually an adolescent girl, and usually one that is troubled emotionally. <br /> <br /> WoD Explanation: Some Poltergeist activity is caused by wraiths or specters using the Arcanos Outrage. However, the strong correlation between Poltergeist activity and young adolescent girls near puberty indicates a response beyond that of free willed activity by the Restless.<br /> <br /> Humans unconsciously generate most Poltergeist activity. Pubescent girls in emotional turmoil awaken it just like wraiths obtain Pathos through their Passions. <br /> <br /> At puberty, the human female first becomes capable of giving birth to life. This influx of life energies creates a tie with the Tempest because of the potential creation of life where nothing before existed. In addition, when combined with intense Passion caused by such adolescent turmoil, the girl is a beacon that draws forces towards her wanting to feed on such Passion. <br /> <br /> The girl\u2019s Shadow is involved in this manifesting this turmoil as the Outrage Arcanos via the Hive Mind. It is directed by the partially awakened Shadow. However, as the girl learns to deal with the changes in her body and becomes comfortable, the Shadow can no longer draw Angst and the activity soon ceases. <br /> <br /> More prolonged Poltergeist activity is the result of her Shadow attracting a Spectre to the girl, probably one already nearby. Other traumatic events might also induce Poltergeist activity, but these are much harder, and more rare. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T22:50:36-07:00","id":1386619,"title":"","content":"Whoah interesting twist on Poltergeists! I might steal this for Changeling and say they generate some sort of Chimera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T14:16:38-07:00","id":1387079,"title":"","content":"I can definitely see that, especially for more mischievous poltergeists as opposed to more terrifying ones.<br /> <br /> This next one isn't really a haunting, but another paranormal phenomenon I think works well with Wraith.<br /> <br /> <b>Spontaneous Human Combustion </b><br /> <br /> Phenomenon: For as yet scientifically unknown reasons, times occur when an unsuspecting person bursts into flames and is incinerated. The flames begin within the victim's own body and reduce their human fuel to a pile of ashes in minutes - sometimes seconds. The whole event is so quick and selective that objects near the victim show only minor heat damage, if any at all. Sometimes, even the victim's clothes are left untouched. <br /> <br /> Classic cases are characterized by five main features: <br /> <br /> 1) The victim's body and clothing is mostly reduced to ash. <br /> 2) Small portions of the body (an arm, a foot, maybe the head) remain unburned. <br /> 3) Only objects immediately associated with the body have burned; the fire never spread away from the body. <br /> 4) A greasy soot deposit covers the ceiling and walls, usually stopping three to four feet above the floor. <br /> 5) Objects above this three to four foot line show signs of heat damage (melted candles, cracked mirrors, etc.); objects below this line show no damage. <br /> <br /> Documentation for such burnings is lacking in non-European descended societies. These burnings have occurred for as long as mankind has existed, but most coroners, pathologists, scientists, and fire officials ignore such evidence: blithely choosing much neater and less controversial explanations for these unexplained deaths. <br /> <br /> WoD Explanation: Cases of spontaneous human combustion are due to an assault upon the living by Oblivion. The living person\u2019s own Shadow partially awakens, and the sudden terror of existence creates a massive surge of Angst. This sparks an intuitive use of Outrage from the Hive Mind that starts self-immolation that burns the body\u2019s fat storage like a candle wick. <br /> <br /> it is not known why the victims are selected. Perhaps some descendant or innocent action would have far-reaching consequence of Fate. However, a mark is put upon them, and some Oracles claim to detect these by the Fatalism Arcanoi. Some experts at the Institute for Obliviographic Studies believe all these incidents are related back to a Malfean whose servants are known as the Flaming Brand Church.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T20:11:25-07:00","id":1390903,"title":"","content":"Here's another classic real world paranormal phenomenon and its explanation in Wraith terms.<br /> <br /> <b>Vortex (Portal) </b><br /> <br /> Phenomenon: Certain areas appear to have doorways or portals to another dimension. The paranormal activity there does not appear to be intelligent hauntings, but distinctly inhuman entities. Very often the vortex is accompanied by strange beings known as Shadow People.<br /> <br /> Manifestations of vortices vary. Daytime \u201corbs\u201d of light, streaks or swirls of mist, and funnels have all been spotted. In addition are inexplicable streaks of shadow. While sometimes noticed when they appear, they are more commonly noticed in photographs after the fact.<br /> <br /> WoD Explanation: Vortices are areas in the Skinlands whose Shadowlands contain Nihils. The Nihils may not be &quot;static&quot; and could flicker into existence and then suddenly end after some amount of time later. The inhuman entities are either Spectres or malevolent Plasmic creatures. The manifestations in the Skinlands are a result of increased presence of Oblivion resulting in a deformity similar to the effects of Pandemonium.<br /> <br /> In the World of Darkness, the manifestations of such vortices might be more severe than those recorded in the real world. Emotions of fear could be stronger, and the color, size and shape of such lighted orbs or mists could be more provocative especially if it precedes an actual manifestation of a Spectre. In places of extreme evil, the living might see numerous swirling bands of shadows, pantomiming human movement, as they orbit around tendrils of deep purple mist at night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}